     1	//! Screen handler module.
     2	//!
     3	//! This module defines the core screen handler system for container UIs.
     4	//! A screen handler manages the server-side state of a container interface,
     5	//! handling slot layout, click processing, item transfer, and synchronization
     6	//! with the client.
     7	//!
     8	//! # Core Components
     9	//!
    10	//! - [`ScreenHandler`] - The main trait for container screen handlers
    11	//! - [`ScreenHandlerBehaviour`] - Shared state for all screen handlers
    12	//! - [`InventoryPlayer`] - Interface for player interactions with containers
    13	//! - [`ScreenProperty`] - Container UI properties (progress bars, etc.)
    14	//!
    15	//! # Screen Handler Lifecycle
    16	//!
    17	//! 1. Creation - Screen handler is created with slots and sync ID
    18	//! 2. Opening - Player opens the container, sync handler attaches
    19	//! 3. Interaction - Click packets are processed, items move between slots
    20	//! 4. Closing - Container closes, cursor item is dropped/given to player
    21	//!
    22	//! # Slot Indexing
    23	//!
    24	//! Slots are indexed from 0 within each screen handler. Special values:
    25	//! - `-1` - Cursor slot (held item)
    26	//! - `-999` - Outside inventory (drop to world)
